{"code":"e1","participant":"e1 saehui","condition":"grid","name":"saehui task 2","id":"f1a5a5fc-a5e3-4356-8d46-c2d252b05031","moments":{"d997ea98-f20a-4099-9ea6-49114a84cb7f":{"videoName":"A001C002_240718OR","startS":14,"endS":25,"notes":"Hi, I'm Viviana matsuda. Um, I do pottery for a living. My brand name is Mud Witch. Um, yeah. I'm a full time potter."},"0b1cf930-3e62-4571-a8b0-34c78ce405d0":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":668.9,"endS":682.5,"notes":"Um, so my voice and style for mud, which it's kind of a funny thing where when I was learning to do ceramics, I was also learning about the body positivity movement."},"4349ae73-65e4-48f6-8894-18746dab4c8c":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":693.9,"endS":702.1,"notes":"And I was like starting to make these like chubby shapes and they're literally called this is the Chubby Mug. This is the Venus mug"},"ba3e1a4b-861a-47e6-8fdb-cb1461f4de1a":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":702.3,"endS":707.8,"notes":"I think those two things kind of just mushed together the learning clay and the body positivity."},"caee06c8-1059-4fd2-9d6b-752d4854719e":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":709.9,"endS":721,"notes":"they were originally supposed to be kind of like an abstract like vision of, of people, like different bodies sitting, dancing, whatever."},"0080bb87-4fb7-4f7f-a373-553f282fa1b8":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":728.5,"endS":737.2,"notes":"so I used like 11 different types of clay, and they were all the range of skin tones. Um, so they were like naked."},"2365676d-e85c-4f1a-bf13-22005ed12ac4":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":738.1,"endS":742.4,"notes":"and then I was like, well, let's slap some color on these, um, let's clothe these babes."},"a57f372d-3d7e-4174-a29e-a6d1d989fac0":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":756,"endS":762,"notes":"I, It started off as one thing, and now it's just like, I just want to make something that, like, makes people smile."},"84c9bbb6-1e6e-49ed-a477-f1b41dcf1286":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":897.6,"endS":906.3,"notes":"Like, there's something called the artist's hand where when you, um, hand-built something or we'll throw it, you can kind of feel where the artist's hands have been."},"c1771688-d185-42ea-a640-0fe561fa5559":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":907.1,"endS":923.6,"notes":"and I think that that is very important because we, you know, in society, we're like, so becoming more and more disconnected to, like human interaction in especially, like, touch or anything along those lines."},"b4f92bc2-f20b-4163-92ca-fe0f2e814dfc":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":1140.9,"endS":1150.9,"notes":"I think that it's so easy to desire so many things, um, that we actually don't need."},"a5960a28-85e8-48a0-8562-172247ec8823":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":1203,"endS":1207.2,"notes":"Um, but also just the value of keeping something for a very long time."},"5103dc13-e586-4808-821b-2726b83080bf":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":1209.2,"endS":1221.1,"notes":"with lockdown, people really sat in their houses and realized that the things that were surrounding them weren't bringing them joy. And I think that's why ceramics has had such a big surge."},"8e3b8d4d-6e17-46be-88ea-07c38bad633b":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":1225.1,"endS":1247.2,"notes":"the pendulum is really swinging in both ways, where people are really like, I want a select few things that I know will bring me happiness in my house. And then the pendulum swings the other way with like extreme fast fashion, temu shi and nonsense, where you can get like 80 mugs for whatever, a doll or whatever."},"4038e308-c469-47f3-8b7d-1c62b9650e98":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":1257.6,"endS":1263.8,"notes":"But not only that, but like, you don't need all of that stuff. Like, you could literally just get a couple things that make you happy."},"192f3dbe-4326-46dc-b07c-2134b3500251":{"videoName":"B003C